y 0 3

      ⍝ Regression: Bugs6 #5 (Blake McBride). IndexExpr never joining
      ⍝ all_index_exprs (so )CHECK's "no stale indices" and
      ⍝ IndexExpr::erase_stale() are permanent no-ops) is currently
      ⍝ deliberate -- see the long comment on IndexExpr's constructor:
      ⍝ actually joining the ring has twice caused a real SIGSEGV
      ⍝ elsewhere (Quad_SYL.tc's )CLEAR, only reproducible via the full
      ⍝ testcase suite, not this file alone) despite passing everything
      ⍝ tried here. This test still has value regardless of which way
      ⍝ that constructor is wired: a rank>=2 literal index whose
      ⍝ evaluation is aborted (error) partway, repeated with )SIC, must
      ⍝ not crash or corrupt anything either way.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      T←4 4⍴⍳16

